      "title": "Time Did the Decorating",
      "text": "Obtain one listed rusted, mossy or weathered material."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Time Did the Decorating",
      "text": "Use age and wear as a deliberate building palette."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Getting started",
      "text": "Find a weathered material or check its available recipe. No fixed waiting period or building age is required."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "How to use it",
      "text": "Expose iron to rain or place bricks near extreme heat. Observe rusting or cracking under the documented environmental systems."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "How to use it",
      "text": "Inspect sand after lightning and use documented lightning block conversions. Lightning can form Fulgurite/Vitrified Sand and convert obsidian to crying obsidian or stone through magma to lava."
    }
  ]
